+# Observed need evidence V1: qualified storage, exact recall usability limit
+
+Core source aa0e74b208ea2f085b1b4b0c77f9fb7b77a0f1d6; integrated fixed-world source578708ef9fc50a3649595b63309750c0cf9d7a5b/tree3addef7648dac6770285e92a190d8981d0361d87. This is an opt-in standalone module with no default activation, old MemoryBank edits, phenotype changes, decoder port, CPU/GPU policy integration or new autonomous allocation.
+
+## Actual observations
+
+Three prescribed Inspect observations use fresh age600 initialization at world tick600, not600 lived ticks. All share maturation .32894737, puberty=false (puberty tick1113), biochemical expression1, loneliness.15, energy.7925, health1, injury0, awake. Earlier 'mature' wording was unsupported and is corrected: these are juvenile fixtures with expressed chemistry.
+
+World rate20Hz. Each registered action measures exactly tick600→601; metabolism cadence6 and development cadence60 ticks. Finalizing that same world interval does not advance its biology again. One passive no-command clone per condition produces the same loneliness change, confirming this is actual ambient contact relief during the interval, not an isolated consequence of Inspect.
+
+| Condition | Social dose | Measured loneliness after−before | Source bytes | One-record store bytes |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| Actual peer contact | .0125 | −.007499993 | 16,241 | 18,027 |
+| Equally positioned toy | 0 | 0 | 15,949 | 17,701 |
+| Separated observed peer | 0 | 0 | 16,130 | 17,916 |
+
+All11 stored deltas match the actual measured physiology bitwise. Measured zero remains known. Duplicate observations reject without increasing count; wrong family and artificial changed-pressure exact queries are Unknown. Save/restore is byte-exact and reproduces the source-context recall. No raw store or patch arrays are included in shared deliverables.
+
+**Actual next-world queries miss in all3 cases.** Target/family identity remains the same; the peer's loneliness is now.14250001, and other interval observations also change. Exact context matching therefore demonstrates binding integrity, not a useful learned recall policy. No creature was reset to hide this limitation. The next-world query executes no extra action or biology interval.
+
+## Contract tests and preserved failures
+
+Final new core suite11/11 passes: Unknown versus measured zero; signed11 lanes; exact identity/context and explicit clock-only invariance; bounded query/age/response; replay guard through prune/restore; byte limits and deterministic eviction; malformed restore even with recomputed envelope integrity; two-channel singleton association/ambiguity; opposite signed records retained independently; populated nonzero-clock context projection.
+
+The original synthetic fixtures failed before store assertions: invalid successor private graph ticks and unsupported unobserved Inspect grounding. A later three-test failure correctly exposed accidental changing maturation/hormones in supposedly identical contexts. Fixtures were corrected without relaxing production validation. A missing test-only ChannelPhysicalOutcome import caused one compile failure. Logs retain all attempts.
+
+The initial world Cargo invocation selected0 tests due a short exact-name filter; it is not counted. Its fully qualified construction check passed1/1. The final store/world check passed1/1 over the three controlled conditions and their passive clones.
+
+Synthetic source11440bytes; one-record store12780bytes. Byte-pressure stress retains16 records at1041350bytes below1048576, with oversized sources rejected atomically. These synthetic sizes differ from the actual world table above.
+
+Legacy memory/query/experience/physiology/golden-digest guard results and final strict lint/fmt results are in the adjacent logs and manifest. No independent source clearance or executed GPU check is claimed. Parent source review prompted the dedicated typed context projection; current nested schema has event identities rather than explicit timestamps, and no current future-dated rejection was reproduced. The revised implementation never builds an impossible earlier frame.
+
+## Interpretation
+
+The complete original source is retained for bounded revalidation, and only raw measured signed drive changes are derived. The store does not identify causal motor contributions, infer social categories, invent past per-need memory, pool opposite effects into zero, or recast every drive as a deficit. Existing accepted state remains untouched. The separately described retrieval experiment is required before any claim that an actual next-world state can use this new evidence.
